refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
boolstream_wrapper_register stringprotocol stringclass intflags0
Allows you to implement your own protocol handlers and streams for use with most filesystem functions (such as fopen, file_exists, scandir, unlink etc.). realpath, chdir, readlink, symlink, link, disk_free_space, tempnam and glob never reach the wrapper.

&reftitle.returnvalues;


 &return.success;


 stream_wrapper_register will return &false; if the
 protocol already has a handler, or if it is not a
 valid scheme name, in which case an E_WARNING is
 emitted.

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;





    8.0.0

     Now throws a TypeError if class
     is not a valid class name. Previously, an E_WARNING
     was raised and &false; was returned.

  &reftitle.examples;



    How to register a stream wrapper


<?php
stream_wrapper_register("var", "VariableStream");
$myvar = "";

$fp = fopen("var://myvar", "r+");

fwrite($fp, "line1\n");
fwrite($fp, "line2\n");
fwrite($fp, "line3\n");

rewind($fp);
while (!feof($fp)) {
    echo fgets($fp);
}
fclose($fp);
var_dump($myvar);

?>


    &example.outputs;


line1
line2
line3
